t` for `*sequence` uses `a.firstOfList` which reads `a.first[n]` for children \u2014 all initialized. Good.\n\nFor `*group` oneOrMore nullable = `a.nullable[x.expr]`. Good.\n\nNow FOLLOW computation. Initialize follow[n] = empty, follow[root] = {EOF}. Iterate:\n```go\nfunc (a *analysis) computeFollowSets(root node) {\n    for _, n := range a.nodes { a.follow[n] = map[firstToken]bool{} }\n    a.follow[root][firstToken{firstEOF, \"\"}] = true\n    for {\n        changed := false\n        for _, n := range a.nodes {\n            switch x := n.(type) {\n            case *sequence:\n                nodes := sequenceNodes(x)\n                for i, child := range nodes {\n                    tail, allNullable := a.firstOfList(nodes[i+1:])\n                    if a.addFollow(child, tail) { changed = true }\n                    if allNullable {\n                        if a.addFollow(child, a.follow[x]) { changed = true }\n                    }\n                }\n            case *disjunction:\n                for _, c := range x.nodes {\n                    if a.addFollow(c, a.follow[x]) { changed = true }\n                }\n            case *group:\n                if a.addFollow(x.expr, a.follow[x]) { changed = true }\n            case *capture:\n                if a.addFollow(x.node, a.follow[x]) { changed = true }\n            case *strct:\n                if a.addFollow(x.expr, a.follow[x]) { changed = true }\n            case *union:\n                for _, m := range x.disjunction.nodes {\n                    if a.addFollow(m, a.follow[x]) { changed = true }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        if !changed { break }\n    }\n}\n```\n\nWait \u2014 there's a subtle issue with `firstOfList` returning `allNullable=true` for an empty tail. For the last element of a sequence, tail is empty \u2192 allNullable=true \u2192 add FOLLOW(seq) to last element. Good. But for firstOfList(empty) returns empty set, allNullable=true. Good.\n\nBut there's another subt